    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured audit event alongside the existing human-readable audit line for owner creation.\n\n**New file \u2014 `OwnerCreatedEvent.java`** (`rest/function/owner/`): an immutable Java `record` `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event}` that:\n- Uses a `static final AtomicLong SEQUENCE` as the app-wide source of `seq`, so it's **monotonically increasing across every create** for the life of the process (survives per-test transaction rollback).\n- Fixes `event` to the constant `\"OWNER_CREATED\"`.\n- Sources the identifier through a single `primaryIdentifier(Owner)` method that currently returns `owner.getCustomerCode()`. This is **the one place** the primary identifier is chosen \u2014 when the customer code is later unified into the memberId, only that method changes and the event automatically carries the memberId.\n- Serializes to JSON via Jackson 3 (`tools.jackson.databind`, the stack the tests already use).\n\n**Modified `AuditOwnerCreated.java`**: after the existing audit line, it emits the event with `AUDIT.info(\"{}\", OwnerCreatedEvent.next(owner, level).toJson())`. Using the `\"{}\"` placeholder form guarantees the exact JSON string is the logged message (no SLF4J brace-parsing surprises), and `level` is now computed once and reused for both the line and the event.\n\n**Verification:** The emitted line is\n`{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`\nwhich satisfies the acceptance test's assertion (one AUDIT line containing `OWNER_CREATED`, the owner id, and the `customerCode`). The full suite passes: **BUILD SUCCESS**, no failures or errors.",
